-# The Knowledge Card
.card.border-0.shadow-sm.border-start.border-4.border-info
  .card-body.p-4

    -# --- Header ---
    .d-flex.align-items-center.mb-3
      .bg-info-subtle.text-info-emphasis.rounded-circle.d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-center.me-3.lh-1{style: "width: 48px; height: 48px"}
        %span.mi.md-24.fill help

      %div
        %h5.fw-bold.text-dark.mb-0 How Groups & Problem Visibility Work
        %small.text-secondary Comprehensive guide to problem visibility, Group Mode, and Group status effects.

    -# --- Section 1: Problem Visibility & Group Association ---
    %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-2 Problem Visibility Rules
    .row.g-3.mb-4
      .col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.bg-light.h-100
          .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.mi.md-20.text-primary.flex-shrink-0 group
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark Grouped Problems
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            When a problem is assigned to any group, it is 
            %strong strictly hidden from users not in that group.
            This restriction applies 
            %strong even when Problem Group Mode is disabled.
            Only active members of that group (and staff) can see and submit to it.

      .col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.bg-light.h-100
          .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.mi.md-20.text-success.flex-shrink-0 public
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark Ungrouped Problems
          %p.small.text-secondary.mb-0
            Problems with 
            %strong no group
            are visible to 
            %strong all users
            when Problem Group Mode is disabled. If Problem Group Mode is enabled, ungrouped problems are hidden from regular students.

    -# --- Section 2: Problem Group Mode (Enabled vs Disabled) ---
    %hr.text-secondary-subtle.my-3/
    .d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-between.mb-2
      %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-0 Problem Group Mode Configuration
      .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2
        %small.text-secondary Current Status:
        - if GraderConfiguration.use_problem_group?
          %span.badge.bg-success-subtle.text-success.border.border-success-subtle On (Enabled)
        - else
          %span.badge.bg-secondary-subtle.text-secondary.border.border-secondary-subtle Off (Disabled)
        = link_to grader_configuration_index_path, class: 'btn btn-outline-secondary btn-xs py-0 px-2' do
          %span.mi.md-14 settings
          Config

    .row.g-3.mb-4
      .col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.h-100{class: GraderConfiguration.use_problem_group? ? 'bg-light' : 'border-primary-subtle bg-primary-subtle bg-opacity-10'}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.badge.bg-secondary Off (Disabled — Default)
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark Open Ungrouped Problems
          %ul.small.text-secondary.mb-0.ps-3
            %li Problems with <strong>no group</strong> are publicly visible to all logged-in students.
            %li Problems assigned to a group remain <strong>scoped only to that group's members</strong>.
            %li Best for standard classes where general problems are open, with special problem sets restricted to specific cohorts.

      .col-md-6
        .p-3.rounded-3.border.h-100{class: GraderConfiguration.use_problem_group? ? 'border-success-subtle bg-success-subtle bg-opacity-10' : 'bg-light'}
          .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2.mb-1
            %span.badge.bg-success On (Enabled)
            %span.fw-bold.text-dark Strict Group Isolation
          %ul.small.text-secondary.mb-0.ps-3
            %li Students <strong>only see problems in groups they belong to</strong>.
            %li Ungrouped problems are <strong>completely hidden</strong> from regular students (only Admins/Setters see them).
            %li Best for multi-course setups or segregated sections where students must only access their own curriculum.

    -# --- Section 3: Group Status (Enabled vs Disabled) ---
    %hr.text-secondary-subtle.my-3/
    %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-2 Group Status: Effects of Enabling & Disabling a Group
    .d-flex.flex-column.gap-2.mb-4
      .p-3.rounded-3.border.bg-light
        .row.g-3
          .col-md-6
            .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2
              %span.mi.md-20.text-success.flex-shrink-0 check_circle
              %div
                %span.fw-bold.text-dark When a Group is Enabled (Active)
                %ul.small.text-secondary.mb-0.ps-3
                  %li <strong>Problem Access:</strong> Members can see and submit to enabled problems in the group.
                  %li <strong>Announcements:</strong> Group-targeted announcements are displayed on members' main page.
                  %li <strong>Scoreboard & Reports:</strong> Member scores are calculated and displayed on group scoreboards and reports.
                  %li <strong>Bulk Actions:</strong> Can be used to bulk-add users or problems in contests and management tools.
          .col-md-6
            .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2
              %span.mi.md-20.text-danger.flex-shrink-0 cancel
              %div
                %span.fw-bold.text-dark When a Group is Disabled (Inactive)
                %ul.small.text-secondary.mb-0.ps-3
                  %li <strong>Problem Access Revoked:</strong> Members lose access to problems scoped solely by this group (cannot view or submit).
                  %li <strong>Announcements Hidden:</strong> Group-specific announcements are hidden from students.
                  %li <strong>Scoreboard Excluded:</strong> Group members and rankings are removed from the group scoreboard and excluded from totals.
                  %li <strong>Settings Intact:</strong> Problems, users, and editor roles are preserved. Admins/editors can safely re-enable the group at any time.

    -# --- Section 4: Fine-Grained Controls ---
    %hr.text-secondary-subtle.my-3/
    %h6.fw-bold.text-dark.small.text-uppercase.mb-2 Fine-Grained Controls Inside a Group
    .row.g-3
      .col-md-6
        .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2
          %span.mi.md-18.text-warning.flex-shrink-0 toggle_on
          %small.text-secondary
            %strong Problem-level Enabled Toggle:
            Within a group's problem list, you can individually enable or disable specific problems without disabling the whole group.
      .col-md-6
        .d-flex.align-items-start.gap-2
          %span.mi.md-18.text-info.flex-shrink-0 person_off
          %small.text-secondary
            %strong Member-level Enabled Toggle:
            Individual user memberships in a group can be toggled on or off to suspend a specific user's group privileges without removing them.
